# GenAI Evidence Hub Paper Screener — Changelog

Compiled from Claude chat history. Dates reflect when each chat session took place.

---

## v1–v16 — Initial build
**2026-08-12** · *Chat: "Meta-analysis paper screening automation tool"*

Built from scratch across 15+ rapid iterations in a single session:

- Core tkinter GUI with four tabs: Single Paper, Batch Upload, Repository, Settings
- Anthropic API integration (Claude Opus) — PDFs submitted as native documents
- JSON + CSV dual repository storage
- Three-criterion screening logic (GenAI Evidence Hub's original hardcoded criteria)
- Batch CSV processing with stop/resume, live per-paper and total elapsed timers
- Automatic metadata extraction from PDFs (title, authors, year, DOI, journal, abstract)
- Paper ID established as the only manually-entered field
- Repository sorted ascending by `paper_id`; duplicate `paper_id` entries overwrite rather than append
- Inclusion cutoff set to 2023 or later
- Added "Unknown" domain as a last-resort fallback
- Criterion 3 expanded (per SME guidance) to weight actual student outcomes (RCTs, learning gains, effect sizes) equally with direct output metrics
- Automated Item Scoring domain updated to include "sometimes synthetic work"
- **Bug fix:** moved `overall_recommendation` to the *last* field in the JSON output schema — previously the model committed to a verdict before reasoning through criteria, then self-corrected in notes; ordering the schema so the verdict comes last forces full analysis first
- **Backend simplification:** removed Ollama/local model support entirely (too slow) — API-only from this point on
- Removed unused imports (`pdfplumber`, `io`) and dead code (`InterruptedError` handler, `if False` branch, duplicate sort key logic, unused palette keys)
- Established standing rule: README must be updated alongside every application change

---

## v17 — Configurable criteria + automated PDF retrieval
**2026-08-12** · *Chat: "Customizable inclusion criteria and automated PDF scraping"*

Files: `app_v17.py`, `criteria_profiles.py` (new), `pdf_resolver.py` (new), `README.md`, `requirements.txt`

- Replaced hardcoded screening logic with a **criteria profile** architecture — inclusion/exclusion rules, prompt rendering, decision logic, CSV shape, and output schema all derive from a structured JSON profile
- Built compiler flow: raw text → Claude-compiled draft → **mandatory human review** before use
- Validator architecturally enforces that every criterion must carry `exclude_if` conditions before it can be saved (guards against the known false-INCLUDE failure mode from free-text criteria)
- Built-in profile encodes the original three GenAI Evidence Hub criteria exactly
- Profile versioning **forks rather than overwrites** when a profile is edited after use
- Added a local decision-rule engine that recomputes recommendations post-API-call, preventing model drift from silently affecting the repository
- New PDF resolution waterfall: direct link → arXiv → Unpaywall → OpenAlex → Semantic Scholar → Europe PMC → `citation_pdf_url` scraping — with per-source toggles, session-level DOI caching, and rate limiting
- Added abstract-only fallback mode (forces UNCLEAR verdicts on anything not explicitly stated, by design produces a higher `MANUAL_REVIEW` rate)
- README and requirements rewritten from scratch to document the profile system, full schema reference, and troubleshooting for the two most likely failure modes

---

## v18 — Local file library & matching engine
**2026-08-13** · *Chats: "Automated paper file mapping and review system" → "Dynamic paper file mapping and upload system"*

Files: `app_v18.py`, `local_library.py` (new, ~900 lines), `criteria_profiles.py` (updated), `pdf_resolver.py` (unchanged), `requirements_v18.txt`, `README_v18.md`

Built to solve locally-held papers with uninformative filenames (e.g. "Download (4).pdf") that can't be found by the open-access resolver.

- **Design correction mid-session:** paper IDs are internal database identifiers with no relation to the paper itself — filename-based ID matching was scrapped. Matching instead reads file *contents* (DOIs, arXiv IDs, titles, author surnames) — filenames treated as the weakest possible signal
- Tiered confidence system (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/NONE): only deterministic identifier matches auto-accept; fuzzy matches require a mandatory human confirmation dialog before any screening runs
- Bijective assignment (one file per paper, one paper per file), greedy scored candidate matching
- File-type support: PDF (`pypdf`), PPTX (OOXML parsing, zero new deps), DOCX, and non-PDF conversion via LibreOffice
- New `extracted_text` screening basis added to `criteria_profiles.py` prompt builders
- New "Local Files" tab: folder picker, optional drag-and-drop (`tkinterdnd2`), match tree, mandatory review dialog with per-file evidence and reassignment UI
- Screening worker records `local_file` / `match_method` / `match_confidence` provenance columns in the repository
- Batch CSV template gained optional `title`/`doi`/`authors`/`year` columns for paywalled papers with no resolvable URL
- Design decisions (author-conflict demotion, DOI-match exemption from that demotion, 0.55 confidence floor, near-tie forcing manual review) reasoned through with SME input before coding
- Fixture suite covering DOI matching, exact/fuzzy title disambiguation, near-identical sibling titles, equidistant fuzzy ambiguity, duplicate file detection, scanned PDFs, filename token boundaries, manual reassignment conflicts
- GUI smoke-tested on Xvfb; caught a real bug (PDF header validation before API submission) and a test-harness bug (conservative toggle state leaking across test cases)
- Added CLI diagnostic interface to `local_library.py`, correcting a false claim inherited from the v17 README

